cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: Membrane Committee
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-21
authors:
  - family-names: Brisson
    given-names: Jean-François
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/membrane-committee"
abstract: >-
  Synthetic toy simulation (classical software, not physical
  holography hardware): a heterogeneous committee of holographic
  membranes at different coarse-graining resolutions voting on
  noisy probes. Negative result: majority, confidence-weighted and
  reliability-weighted voting do not beat the best single member at
  low-to-moderate noise and only marginally exceed it near chance,
  while the oracle gap shows the ensemble holds unused information.
keywords:
  - holographic-memory
  - ensemble
  - heterogeneity
  - voting
  - negative-result
